]}, {"recommendationid": "231696370", "author": {"steamid": "76561198043467370", "personaname": "Yashimasta", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Yashimasta/", "num_games_owned": 164, "num_reviews": 50, "playtime_forever": 1246, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1246, "last_played": 1785440966, "avatar": "733affc91d33625d3d67cd9a012d9023c6a66f9c"}, "language": "english", "review": "Amazing and smooth combat gameplay.... but then the devs decided to add in their own cursed problem: locking gadgets (powerful permanent perks like Jetpack, Grappling Hook) behind NON-COMBAT gameplay. Find a shovel, run around and dig graves until you find the \"right one\" (just RNG). Find a specific Gun and give it an NPC , repeat multiple times with multiple different Guns. No where on the Store Page does it say you'll need to perform a slog of tasks in order to have the expected tools needed, it is seriously baffling that these aren't just Perks you unlock at the Basecamp.\n\nFROM THE WIKI:\n\"The Cooking Gloves are a Gadget hidden in Fields, which, when enabled, reduces the cost to upgrade weapons or reroll their affixes at Chef Paul by 1 for weapons whose Cards are unlocked. To unlock them, the player has to to show the requested weapons (in order: Blunderbuzz, Junk Rifle, Sheriff's Carbine) to the Snapshot Sam in the break area of Fields. Once they are unlocked, their effect can be turned off and on at the Gadget Rack.\"\n\nI've played exclusively on Hard Mode, greatly enjoyed getting to the final Boss multiple times, but now I am faced with looking up multiple guides and specifically playing to not win in order to unlock the rest of the Gadgets (I have 4 right now) so I have a chance to beat the final boss. That's not why I bought this game, I bought it for the slick gunplay - so no....I don't think I will....", "timestamp_created": 1785445852, "timestamp_updated": 1785445852, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 